    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0636" n="624" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg624"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.404/8–845</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-08">August 8, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Mr. Novikov<anchor n="38" xml:id="d402-f1"/> then told me informally and not as
                    an official communication that in ten minutes from now, at three p.m. Washington
                    time, 10 p.m., Moscow time, Mr. Molotov<anchor n="39" xml:id="d402-f2"/> would
                    make a declaration stating that Soviet Russia is in a state of war with
                        Japan.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d402-f3"/> I asked Mr. Novikov when the state
                    of war would take effect and he said “tomorrow”. I said, “That will evidently
                    give the Japanese two hours to get ready.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d402-f1" n="38" xml:id="d402-f1-content">
                <p>Nikolay Vassilyevich Novikov, Soviet Chargé.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d402-f2" n="39" xml:id="d402-f2-content">
                <p>Vyacheslav Mikhailovich Molotov, People’s Commissar for Foreign Affairs of the
                    Soviet Union.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d402-f3" n="40" xml:id="d402-f3-content">
                <p>For statement handed by Commissar Molotov to the Japanese Ambassador in the
                    Soviet Union, Naotake Sato, on August 8, see footnote 1, document 1382, <ref
                        target="frus1945Berlinv02#pg_1474">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Conference of Berlin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Potsdam</hi>), vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p.
                    1474</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
